`pypdfium2` bundles a prebuilt PDFium. PDFium is BSD-3-Clause and carries its own bundled
dependency notices; the wheel ships them under
`.../site-packages/pypdfium2_raw/` and `pypdfium2*.dist-info/licenses/`. Those files must stay
present in the image distribution — do not strip licence files from site-packages.

PyMuPDF / MuPDF (import name `fitz`) is **not** used and must not be reintroduced: it is
AGPL-3.0 unless separately licensed, which is incompatible with this proprietary hosted
service. `tests/test_renderer_licensing.py` fails if it re-enters requirements.txt, the
sources, the Dockerfile, the deploy YAML, or the installed environment.


